+# PERF provenance — S45..S48 benchmark claims (hard data trail)
+
+Every performance number quoted in the S45–S48 sessions traces to a
+measurement recorded here. This file exists because "faster" claims
+without a reproducible trail are worthless; where a number could not be
+measured on this box it is marked as such.
+
+Machine of record: 2-core research VM (Ice Lake-class uarch), 4 GB RAM,
+gcc 14.2 as the local reference compiler. Wall-clock timing via
+`date +%s%N` around whole-process runs (the box has no perf counters);
+each figure below is the median of ≥3 reps after one discarded warm-up,
+dev server stopped during all measurements.
+
+## S48 — chacha20_block: the 2.19x EPYC report, attributed
+
+**The report.** Zen 5 EPYC, plain `-O2`, no `-march`: LCCC 332.21 ms vs
+GCC 16.2 at 152.00 ms (ratio 2.1914x).
+
+**Attribution (no guesswork):**
+
+1. *Not a regression from the merged series.* Base `93596224` (pre-S47)
+   and post-merge main were built side by side; `chacha20_core` asm was
+   **byte-identical** (0 diff lines). The ratio change is on the
+   reference side: GCC 16.2 vectorizes chacha at plain `-O2`, the local
+   GCC 14.2 does not — the user's 152 ms is a vectorized kernel, and
+   332/152 ≈ 2.19 is the vectorization gap of a scalar-shaped kernel,
+   not a new slowdown.
+2. *Local arithmetic cross-check.* Local GCC-scalar runs 226 ms; the
+   user's GCC 152 ms ⇒ machine-speed ratio ≈ 1.49, which predicts
+   LCCC default ≈ 235 ms on the EPYC — i.e. the LCCC binary itself runs
+   ~2.1x above what its cycle count should be there. Local (chain-bound
+   host): LCCC vector kernel ≈ dead even with GCC scalar; the EPYC
+   (throughput-bound, Zen 5) exposes the per-double-round op count.
+
+**Hand-written asm variant lab** (RFC 7539 §2.3.2-verified shapes, the
+design basis for the landed fixes; lab sources transcribed from the
+compiler's own output and hand-optimised):
+
+| variant | ms | Δ vs shipped |
+|---|---|---|
+| v0 — exact transcription of the current compiler loop | 232 | — |
+| v1 — loop restructure only (no phi copies, in-place state) | 232 | 0% |
+| v3 — v1 + lean prologue (.rodata masks, register state, no staging) | 208 | −10.3% |
+| v4 — v3 + `vprold` (AVX-512F+VL) | 169 | −27.2% |
+| gcc 14.2 `-O2` (scalar; local reference) | 225 | — |
+
+Findings that drove the implementation order: the 6-`vpshufd` loop
+structure is at the dataflow floor for this lane-transpose formulation
+(same views v1 uses); the phi copies are FREE on a chain-bound host
+(v1 ≡ v0) but structurally dominant on throughput-bound hosts; the
+**prologue was the crime scene** — per-call × 2M calls: masks rebuilt
+from four GPR immediates (movd/punpck chains) and the whole state staged
+through store→load slot chains (0xd0-byte frame).
+
+## S48 — landed changes and measured results
+
+1. **W1 — dwordx4 constant-pool flavour** (`emit.rs`):
+   `VecPackI32x4` with four constant lanes lowers to one aligned
+   `movdqa .LvcN(%rip)`; pool flushed `.p2align 4`, sorted by lane set.
+2. **W2a — SSE-128 chain-collector copy-source propagation**
+   (`regalloc.rs::collect_sse128_chain_values`): Copy sources feeding
+   chain values become chain candidates (fixpoint over copy webs), so
+   the preheader `VecLoad`s home in registers instead of frame slots.
+   Sound because the destructive allocator interference-checks every
+   grant. Measured: chacha20_core frame 0xd0 → 0x60 bytes; the 8-entry
+   staging dance (store+reload per state vector) is gone — state loads
+   land directly in xmm10..xmm13.
+3. **W3 — AVX-512VL `vprold`** (`emit.rs`, `intrinsics.rs`,
+   `vectorize.rs`, both ARX passes, `CodegenOptions::avx512vl` plumbed
+   from the existing `-mavx512vl` driver flag): EVEX.128 rotate is one
+   uop where the VEX path spends vpsrld+vpslld+vpor; both ARX
+   vectorizers bypass the pshufb masks when F+VL are available (the
+   xmm form of vprold is #UD on F-only parts such as KNL — the emitter
+   ANDs F && VL && ymm).
+
+**Measured on the landed tree** (medians of 3, this box):
+
+| build | ms |
+|---|---|
+| default `-O2` (was 235 pre-S48) | **230** |
+| `-O2 -march=native` (vprold path, 8 vprold/double-round, 0 pshufb) | **188** (−20%, 17% under gcc-scalar) |
+| gcc 14.2 `-O2` | 225 |
+
+Instruction count: 121 instructions in `chacha20_core` (was ~160 with
+staging + GPR mask builds).
+
+### Deferred rocks (designed, not landed — ranked by expected value)
+
+- **W2b — latch phi-copy handoff.** The loop still carries 4
+  `vmovdqa` phi-copies at the latch. The destructive allocator's
+  `death_from` map is dest-keyed (single edge) but a loop value has TWO
+  copy-defs (preheader + latch); extending the handoff-edge construction
+  to the latch edge is the fix. Deferred: measured ZERO local gain
+  (chain-bound host hides the copies) and it touches the highest-risk
+  allocator machinery; the EPYC (throughput-bound) should see it.
+- **W5 — copy-in forwarding.** `x[]` is copied element-wise into the
+  working state before the loop (scalar copy loop feeding vector
+  packs); the lab's v3 skipped it by loading `in[]` directly into the
+  vector registers (overlap-safe: all reads before any store). This is
+  a middle-end pass concern (cross-loop forwarding), est. the remaining
+  ~20 ms of the local gap to the v3 lab shape.
+- **Feed-loop register forwarding.** The epilogue round-trips the
+  result through memory for the `out[i] = x[i] + in[i]` feed loop.
+
+## Benchmark methodology (unchanged, restated for the record)
+
+Randomised compiler order within each paired round; warm-ups excluded;
+median wall time; paired bootstrap CI where quoted; no automatic
+outlier removal; CPU pinning (taskset, cpu 0) on the benchmark runner.
+`>= 9` reps for any benchmark whose run is < 20 ms (decision-grade
+noise floor on this box).
